---
// LocalStack · Reference — CLI + Terraform + SDK cookbook (Python/TS columns).
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "LocalStack · Cookbook CLI + Terraform";
const titleEn = "LocalStack · CLI + Terraform Cookbook";
const titleFallback = "LocalStack · Cookbook CLI + Terraform";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
];
---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow"
          ><span data-lang="pt">⬡ Referência · Cookbook</span
          ><span data-lang="en">⬡ Reference · Cookbook</span></span
        >
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">O cookbook: CLI, SDK e Terraform</span
          ><span data-lang="en">The cookbook: CLI, SDK and Terraform</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >A essência comprimida das 7 lições: <strong>um comando por
            intenção</strong>, a mesma operação nas duas linguagens, e o bloco
            provider que nunca mais você precisa procurar. Lições vão e vêm —
            este doc fica.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The compressed essence of the 7 lessons: <strong>one command per
            intent</strong>, the same operation in both languages, and the
            provider block you will never search for again. Lessons come and
            go — this doc stays.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Bootstrap diário</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Daily bootstrap</span>
      </h2>
      <pre class="block"><code>docker start localstack                  <span class="c"># container de pé</span>
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test             <span class="c"># credenciais falsas</span>
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
awslocal sts get-caller-identity          <span class="c"># "vivo?" — sempre rode antes</span>
<span class="c"># alternativa moderna p/ SDKs: export AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566</span></code></pre>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Uma intenção, três formas</span
        ><span data-lang="en">One intent, three forms</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>S3 · criar bucket</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># CLI</span>
awslocal s3 mb s3://b1
<span class="c"># Python</span>
boto3.client(<span class="s">"s3"</span>, endpoint_url=END)\
  .create_bucket(Bucket=<span class="s">"b1"</span>)
<span class="c"># TypeScript</span>
<span class="k">new</span> S3Client({ endpoint: END, region: <span class="s">"us-east-1"</span>,
  credentials: { accessKeyId: <span class="s">"test"</span>,
    secretAccessKey: <span class="s">"test"</span> } })</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>S3 · upload</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># CLI</span>
awslocal s3 cp a.txt s3://b1/a.txt
<span class="c"># Python</span>
s3.put_object(Bucket=<span class="s">"b1"</span>,
  Key=<span class="s">"a.txt"</span>, Body=<span class="s">"x"</span>.encode())
<span class="c"># TypeScript</span>
<span class="k">await</span> s3.send(<span class="k">new</span> PutObjectCommand({
  Bucket: <span class="s">"b1"</span>, Key: <span class="s">"a.txt"</span>,
  Body: <span class="s">"x"</span> }))</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>SQS · consumir + apagar</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># CLI</span>
awslocal sqs receive-message --queue-url URL
awslocal sqs delete-message --queue-url URL \
  --receipt-handle RH
<span class="c"># Python</span>
m = sqs.receive_message(QueueUrl=u)[
        <span class="s">"Messages"</span>][0]
sqs.delete_message(QueueUrl=u,
  ReceiptHandle=m[<span class="s">"ReceiptHandle"</span>])
<span class="c"># TypeScript</span>
<span class="k">const</span> [m] = ( <span class="k">await</span> sqs.send(
  <span class="k">new</span> ReceiveMessageCommand(
    { QueueUrl: u }))).Messages!;
<span class="k">await</span> sqs.send(<span class="k">new</span> DeleteMessageCommand(
  { QueueUrl: u, ReceiptHandle: m.ReceiptHandle! }));</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>DynamoDB · contador</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># CLI</span>
awslocal dynamodb get-item \
  --table-name visitas \
  --key <span class="s">'{"path":{"S":"/home"}}'</span>
<span class="c"># Python</span>
db.update_item(TableName=t,
  Key={<span class="s">"path"</span>: {<span class="s">"S"</span>: p}},
  UpdateExpression=<span class="s">"ADD visitas :um"</span>,
  ExpressionAttributeValues={
    <span class="s">":um"</span>: {<span class="s">"N"</span>: <span class="s">"1"</span>}})
<span class="c"># TypeScript</span>
<span class="k">await</span> db.send(<span class="k">new</span> UpdateItemCommand({
  TableName: t, Key: { path: { S: p } },
  UpdateExpression: <span class="s">"ADD visitas :um"</span>,
  ExpressionAttributeValues:
    { <span class="s">":um"</span>: { N: <span class="s">"1"</span> } } }));</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Lambda — os 8 comandos que cobrem 95%</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Lambda — the 8 commands covering 95%</span>
      </h2>
      <pre class="block"><code>awslocal lambda create-function --function-name f \
  --runtime python3.12 --handler lambda_function.handler \
  --zipfile fileb://function.zip --role arn:aws:iam::000000000000:role/R

awslocal lambda invoke --payload <span class="s">'{"a":1}'</span> \
  --cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out out.json &amp;&amp; cat out.json

awslocal lambda update-function-code --function-name f \
  --zipfile fileb://function.zip
awslocal lambda update-function-configuration --function-name f \
  --environment <span class="s">"Variables={K=V}"</span>

awslocal logs tail /aws/lambda/f --since 5m
awslocal lambda get-function-configuration --function-name f \
  --query Environment.Variables
awslocal lambda delete-function --function-name f</code></pre>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Terraform — o bloco e o loop</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Terraform — the block and the loop</span>
      </h2>
      <pre class="block"><code>pip install terraform-local        <span class="c"># wrapper `tflocal`</span>
tflocal init | plan | apply -auto-approve | destroy -auto-approve

<span class="c"># provider manual (sem tflocal) — s3_use_path_style é obrigatório</span>
<span class="k">provider</span> <span class="s">"aws"</span> {
  access_key                  = <span class="s">"test"</span>
  secret_key                  = <span class="s">"test"</span>
  region                      = <span class="s">"us-east-1"</span>
  s3_use_path_style           = <span class="k">true</span>
  skip_credentials_validation = <span class="k">true</span>
  skip_metadata_api_check     = <span class="k">true</span>
  <span class="k">endpoints</span> {
    s3       = <span class="s">"http://s3.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566"</span>
    lambda   = <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>
    sqs      = <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>
    sns      = <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>
    dynamodb = <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>
  }
}</code></pre>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">URLs locais &amp; limites do plano grátis</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Local URLs &amp; free-tier limits</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>
            <span data-lang="pt">URLs que importam</span
            ><span data-lang="en">URLs that matter</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            <code>S3: http://localhost:4566/&lt;bucket&gt;/&lt;key&gt;</code><br />
            <code>S3 alt: http://s3.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566/…</code><br />
            <code>API GW: http://&lt;apiId&gt;.execute-api.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566/&lt;stage&gt;/&lt;path&gt;</code><br />
            <code>API GW alt: http://localhost:4566/_aws/execute-api/&lt;apiId&gt;/&lt;stage&gt;/&lt;path&gt;</code><br />
            <code>SQS queue-url: http://localhost:4566/000000000000/&lt;fila&gt;</code>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>
            <span data-lang="pt">Community (grátis) vs pago</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Community (free) vs paid</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"><strong>Grátis:</strong> S3, Lambda, SQS,
            SNS, DynamoDB (+Streams), API GW v1, IAM, CloudWatch Logs,
            Secrets Manager, Route53.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"><strong>Free:</strong> S3, Lambda, SQS,
            SNS, DynamoDB (+Streams), API GW v1, IAM, CloudWatch Logs,
            Secrets Manager, Route53.</span
            ><br />
            <span data-lang="pt"><strong>Pagos:</strong> RDS, ECR, API GW
            v2 (HTTP/WebSocket) — veja a comparação oficial.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"><strong>Paid:</strong> RDS, ECR, API GW
            v2 (HTTP/WebSocket) — check the official comparison.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Regra final de depuração: <strong>quando algo falhar, rode
          primeiro <code>sts get-caller-identity</code></strong> (container
          vivo?) e <code>logs tail</code> (o que a função viu?). Nove em dez
          mistérios morrem aí.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Final debugging rule: <strong>when something fails, first run
          <code>sts get-caller-identity</code></strong> (container alive?)
          and <code>logs tail</code> (what did the function see?). Nine out
          of ten mysteries die there.</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/connecting/aws-cli/">awslocal</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/localstack/terraform-local">tflocal</a> ·
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/services/apigateway/">URLs do API GW</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.localstack.cloud/pricing-comparison">planos</a>
      </p>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt">Fontes:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Sources:</span>
          <a href="../RESOURCES.md">recursos do tópico</a>
        </div>
        <a class="next-card" href="../lessons/0001-localstack-up.html"
          ><span class="lbl"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Recomeçar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Start over</span></span
          >
          <div class="t">
            <span data-lang="pt">Lição 1 — LocalStack no Docker →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Lesson 1 — LocalStack in Docker →</span>
          </div></a
        >
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Algo não ficou claro? Pergunte ao agente — ele é seu
            professor.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Anything unclear? Ask the agent—your teacher.</span
          >
          · <a href="../../../index.html">⬡ Hub</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
